@startuml Component Diagram - Simulador API
title Diagrama de Componentes — API de Simulación (Fastify Container) — Nivel 3
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 10
skinparam titleFontSize 11
skinparam rectangleFontSize 10
skinparam ArrowFontSize 10
skinparam NoteFontSize 10
skinparam wrapWidth 190
skinparam nodesep 6
skinparam ranksep 18
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #666666
  ArrowColor #666666
  FontColor white
}

rectangle "**Desarrollador / Tester QA**\n\nEjecuta pruebas y dispara\nwebhooks" as Dev #1F4E79
rectangle "**Frontend del Comercio**\n\nConsume la API REST\npara iniciar pagos" as Frontend #A9A9A9
rectangle "**Aplicacion del Comercio**\n\nRecibe webhooks firmados" as Comercio #A9A9A9
rectangle "**SDK Kit Pagos**\n\nFachada llamada por\nla capa REST" as SDK #A9A9A9

rectangle "API de Simulacion (Fastify / Node.js 18+)\n[container]" as System #FFFFFF;text:black {
  rectangle "**Kit Pagos REST API**\n<i>[Fastify Plugin /</i>\n<i>TypeScript]</i>\n<i>kit-pagos-api/</i>\n\nExpone /v1/api.\nValida DTOs y delega\noperaciones al SDK" as RestApi #2E75B6
  rectangle "**HTTP Routers de**\n**Simulacion**\n<i>[Fastify Plugins /</i>\n<i>TypeScript]</i>\n<i>routes/</i>\n\nExpone\n/v1/sim/{pasarela}/*.\nElige escenarios y\nconstruye respuestas\nnativas simuladas" as Router #2E75B6
  rectangle "**CredentialResolver y**\n**KitPagosProvider**\n<i>[Servicios /</i>\n<i>TypeScript]</i>\n\nResuelve credenciales\ny provee instancias\ndel SDK" as Provider #2E75B6
  rectangle "**Webhook Trigger**\n**Endpoint**\n<i>[REST Endpoint</i>\n<i>TypeScript]</i>\n\nPOST\n/v1/sim/webhooks/trigger.\nInvocacion manual\ncon API_AUTH_TOKEN;\nemision automatica\nopcional" as WebhookEndpoint #2E75B6
  rectangle "**OpenAPI Provider**\n<i>[@fastify/swagger + UI]</i>\n\nGenera OpenAPI 3.0.3\ny sirve Swagger UI\nen /docs" as OpenAPI #2E75B6
  rectangle "**Gateway Mock Factory**\n<i>[Factory Pattern</i>\n<i>TypeScript]</i>\n\nConstruye payloads\nJSON emulando Wompi,\nRapyd, Mercado Pago\ny Kushki" as MockFactory #2E75B6
  rectangle "**Signature Generator**\n<i>[Security Utility</i>\n<i>Node.js Crypto]</i>\n\nCalcula firmas\ncriptograficas\n(SHA-256, HMAC)" as SignatureGen #2E75B6
  rectangle "**Transaction Store**\n<i>[In-Memory Store /</i>\n<i>TypeScript]</i>\n<i>store/TransactionStore.ts</i>\n\nAlmacena transacciones\nsimuladas indexadas\npor ID nativo para\nconsultas posteriores\nde estado" as Store #FFE0B2;text:black
}

Frontend --> RestApi : Patron 2\n[HTTPS\n/v1/api]
Comercio --> SDK : Patron 1:\nBackend -> SDK
RestApi --> Provider : Resuelve\ngateway y\ncredenciales
Provider --> SDK : Invocacion local\n[KitPagos]
SDK --> Router : Patron 2:\nllamada HTTP\nal simulador\nen el mismo\nproceso o\ndespliegue
SDK --> Router : Patron 1:\nmodo\nsimulacion\n[HTTP\n/v1/sim]
Dev --> Router : Headers control\n[HTTPS]
Dev --> WebhookEndpoint : Solicita webhook\n[HTTPS]
Dev --> OpenAPI : Explora /docs\n[HTTPS]

Router --> MockFactory : Construye respuesta
MockFactory --> SignatureGen : Solicita firma
WebhookEndpoint --> SignatureGen : Solicita firma
MockFactory --> Store : Guarda\ntransaccion\nsimulada
Router --> Store : Consulta estado

note bottom of RestApi
  Frontera intencional: /v1/api
  vive en kit-pagos-api/,
  separado de routes/ que
  implementa /v1/sim.
end note

note bottom of SDK
  Patron 3, Frontend -> SDK
  unificado de pasarelas: futuro,
  no implementado. Viabilidad en
  investigacion (#110).
end note

note bottom of MockFactory
  "PayU" reemplazado por "Rapyd"
  tras la adquisicion (ver
  architecture-log.md, punto 15/17).
end note

@enduml
